{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/897856-how-did-you-guys-solve-the-issue-with-the-moon-calender","id":897856,"title":"How did you guys solve the issue with the moon calender","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-24T08:48:45-07:00","id":897856,"title":"How did you guys solve the issue with the moon calender","content":"After looking at a moon calendar i realized that the phases vary quite a bit. A full moon last lasts 1-3 nights while others last 8 - this means that a Ahroun can insta-fill their Rage on 3 nights a month and has to suffer from the -1 difficulty on his/her ragerolls on those nights as well. How did you reconcile it or is it fair and balanced? <br /> <br /> Wouldn't that also lead to a rather abysmal Ahroun/Ragabash population as we would have only 10% each?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:02:39-07:00","id":897867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/897856-how-did-you-guys-solve-the-issue-with-the-moon-calender#post897856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After looking at a moon calendar i realized that the phases vary quite a bit. A full moon last lasts 1-3 nights while others last 8 - this means that a Ahroun can insta-fill their Rage on 3 nights a month and has to suffer from the -1 difficulty on his/her ragerolls on those nights as well. How did you reconcile it or is it fair and balanced?<br /> <br /> Wouldn't that also lead to a rather abysmal Ahroun/Ragabash population as we would have only 10% each?</div> </div> </div> </div>It varies. IMW, there are 5 nights of the New Moon, followed by 3 nights each of the waxing phases, followed by 5 nights of the Full Moon, followed by 3 nights each of the waning phases, which comes out to 28 days and either 5 or 6 days of each phase.<br /> <br /> In other games, it is actually a plot point that there are fewer nights of the New and Full Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:26:42-07:00","id":897886,"title":"","content":"That is a nice solution! I am seriously thinking about stealing that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What do you mean exactly when you talk about a plot point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:17:33-07:00","id":898069,"title":"","content":"Imbalance is interesting. You could build your setting off the fact that every month, all the Ahrouns have the same birthday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:35:02-07:00","id":898093,"title":"","content":"It can also be used to play into certain aspects of Garou culture that are kind of hand-waved.<br /> <br /> Ahrouns are commonly portrayed as being natural leaders of a warrior culture, even if the Philodox are mechanically superior in many way (esp. outside of combat). If the Ahrouns are more rare, it helps explain their preferential cultural treatment. If there's 2-3 Philodox for every Ahroun, most Philodox are destined to be in support positions as it is, and Ahrouns skilled in leading battles, and destroying enemies are carry more weight because there's less of them.<br /> <br /> Ragabash being more rare can also highlight well.. how stupid the Garou tend to be as a people. There aren't enough Ragabash around to regularly ask the right questions to do their duty and keep everything going in a more even fashion. How many pointless and/or counter-productive battles could have been avoided with a better representation of the Ragabash in Garou Society?<br /> <br /> Both ways you could use an imbalanced moon calendar as a plot hook.<br /> <br /> Though I default to the 5/6/6/6/5 split in most of my games if it even matters. I've been in a few games where the moon-phase was picked at random (there was even an Auspice die produced back in the day) for any night where it wasn't purposefully scheduled for a given moon phase; but these where games where there was a standing assumption of weeks to months of downtime between major events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T19:04:41-07:00","id":898486,"title":"","content":"To a degree, what constitutes &quot;full&quot;, &quot;gibbous&quot;, 'half&quot;, &quot;crescent&quot;, and &quot;new&quot; is debatable. Every culture defines the phases of the moon in its own way. Technically speaking, the West defines lunar phases in four, not five (New Moon, 1st Quarter, Full Moon, and Last Quarter) except when we decide its eight ((New Moon, Waxing Cescent, 1st Quarter, Waxing Gibbous, Full Moon, Waning Gibbous, Last Quarter, and Waning Crescent). Hawaiians divide up the lunar phases into 30. Not sure how others do it.<br /> <br /> If we want something completely related to mathematics of lunar illumination, it'll be very specific how long each phase lasts. But who knows how Luna decided to define them at the dawn of the world? She could say I don't care if the moon is not fully illuminated, the full moon phase is 5 days. And then divide up each phase equally as 5/6/6/6/5 as others have done. Or if you want, it can be very strict and have what constitutes as New Moon or Full Moon to be less than the others. Each has its own implications.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, since the birth of true Garou are rare and not reflecting the general population, even if the lunar phases are not equal, those born Garou can still be about equal in percentage even though the actually nights available are not equal. If this really is Luna is choosing each Garou's auspice, then the actual birth will happen whenever Luna/Gaia decides it will happen. This means one's auspice is less chance than destiny, but that will work for many games.<br /> <br /> I don't think this is really an important issue, but if it is for your gaming group of chronicle idea, you can hash it out with your group and figure out how it works in your world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T02:33:12-07:00","id":903355,"title":"","content":"For lunar calendar i use this website : <a href=\"https://werwolf-live.de/calendar.php\" target=\"_blank\">https://werwolf-live.de/calendar.php</a>.<br /> If you look at it, it's probably not the exact truth, but it's quite equals about the numbers of moon/auspice. In addition you have the werewolf correspondance for the dates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T03:54:37-07:00","id":903381,"title":"","content":"Isn't that heinrichs group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T23:26:31-07:00","id":906999,"title":"","content":"I reckon I read somewhere all 5 Auspices are about equal. Werewolf Auspices and births are regulated by destiny and miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T07:06:26-07:00","id":908312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/897856-how-did-you-guys-solve-the-issue-with-the-moon-calender?p=906999#post906999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reckon I read somewhere all 5 Auspices are about equal. Werewolf Auspices and births are regulated by destiny and miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your second sentence. But it does not guarantee the first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T02:46:14-07:00","id":918520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/897856-how-did-you-guys-solve-the-issue-with-the-moon-calender?p=903355#post903355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For lunar calendar i use this website : <a href=\"https://werwolf-live.de/calendar.php\" target=\"_blank\">https://werwolf-live.de/calendar.php</a>.<br /> If you look at it, it's probably not the exact truth, but it's quite equals about the numbers of moon/auspice. In addition you have the werewolf correspondance for the dates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for using the calendar....<br /> <br /> But, reconsidering the whole thing, I still can't wrap my head around it....<br /> <br /> The calendar is meant to start on the 1st full moon after the spring equinox. That can be any date from the equinox itself up to 29 days later, when there was a full moon right before the equinox.<br /> <br /> 355 days later the calendar is about to start again, but the calendar hasn't necessarily reached the equinox by then. If the year started two days after the equinox then a lunar year later we reach the end of the year and are still 8 days shy of the equinox when the full moon that is supposed to start a new year occurs.<br /> <br /> So, is the calendar as presented in Rage across the Havens actually working?<br /> If yes, what am I missing?<br /> Is there an adjustment period or is the calendar to drift and the &quot;start&quot; at the first full moon after the equinox is just plain wrong. I read that the Saudi-Calendar drifts and is in sync with the solar calendar only every 33 years.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to fix the garou calendar calculation on the page...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}